            <p class="P1block">All customers served directly by the City and located outside the City limits shall pay at a rate of one hundred ten percent (110%) times the rate for the same classification of service inside the City.</p>

            <p class="P1block">In the case of one (1) meter serving a user that has different classifications of business, the Director shall be authorized to adjust the rate per one thousand (1,000) gallons based upon the contribution of each classification.</p>

            <p class="P1block">The user shall be determined according to customer class or wastewater solids characteristics (see rate schedule above).</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Capacity Charges.</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A capacity charge, as prescribed below, shall be assessed upon:</p>

            <p class="P3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Initial connection to the municipal sewer system; or</p>

            <p class="P3">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any subsequent expansion or modification of the user&rsquo;s building or facility which results in an increased contribution to the sewer system from:</p>

            <p class="P4">(1)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For single- or multifamily residential users, an increase in the number of residential units; or</p>

            <p class="P4">(2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For commercial or industrial users, an increase in the number of fixture units.</p>

            <p class="P3">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Size of water meter installed on the property.</p>

            <p class="P3">d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Each additional water meter added will require additional sewer capacity fees unless specifically designated as a landscape meter.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The capacity charges for the various types of users are as follows:</p>

            <p class="P3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Customer (capacity) charge, dollars.</p>

            <p class="P3">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Residential.</p>

            <p class="P3">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Single-family residential and townhomes (per unit):</p>

